        "text": "The waterlily is a bush tucker of the Aboriginal people in northern Australia. The tuber, stem, flowers and seeds are all edible.\nLike other species in the genus, the plant contains the psychoactive alkaloid aporphine, which provide sedative effects when ingested.",
